cp /glade/u/home/klindsay/dp_asd/SourceMods/src.pop2/* .


Nan,

In order to reduce the volume of ocean model output in the ASD DP runs as Steve, Matt, and I have discussed,
please copy the following 4 files from /glade/u/home/klindsay/dp_asd/SourceMods/src.pop
ocn.base.tavg.csh
ocn.cfc.tavg.csh
ocn.ecosys.tavg.csh
ocn.iage.tavg.csh
to $CASEROOT/SourceMods/src.pop2

These mods
1) reduce the frequency of ocean daily output, base and ecosys, to 5 days
2) remove from BGC ann mean output the tracer budget terms, except for O2, whose terms are retained
3) remove tracer budget terms for CFC11, CFC12, and IAGE

The ocn.ecosys.tavg.csh includes the mods that I previously provided to Nan for the DP runs that were done at NERSC.
These mods removed 8 BGC vars related to carbonate chemistry from the ocean monthly output.

A complication with the 5-day means is that POP's handling of having multiple time slices per file doesn't play friendly with submissions starting and stopping on non-file boundaries. When POP restarts, it always starts a new multi-time slice file, even if the restart date is not a a file boundary. If the restart date is mid-time averaging period, POP will correctly compute the 5 day mean from tavg restarts, but the restarted mean will always go into a new file. POP won't reopen an incomplete file and add more time slices. With the ASD DP runs not starting on 1 Jan, lining up multiple slices of 5-day means with anticipated model restart dates is tricky. So to avoid uneven number of time slices per file, I've simply set up the scripts to write a single time slice to each file.

